Subject: [PATCH 11341/11362] Record the 27B grammar trial result before its
 branch can be lost

The measurement lives on worktree-agent-ad2b64c85092d00d3 and nowhere in main.
The old grammar admitted the empty shell -- confirmed against llama.cpp's own
test-gbnf-validator, not this project's reader -- so the recorded zero-engine
result was a grammar artifact and was never a 27B result.

Trial on GPU 1, n=7 per arm, seed 7: control 7/7 non-trivial at 28,027 decode
tokens and 810 s; grammar 5/7 at 5,980 tokens and 259 s, 28/28 envelopes parsed,
13 submissions, sb26 reaching 1.0 held-out at 422 tokens against the control's
0.946 at 2,539. That is 4.7x fewer tokens and 3.1x faster on a metric that squares
efficiency.

The confound is recorded with the result: every grammar cell took the cheapest
legal envelope first and submitted only after the force nudge, so unprompted
submission is unmeasured. The round-2 grammar has never run against a model.

Also records yesterday's close (36 OK, 18 WARN, 13 GATE_BLOCK, 12 FAIL, 12 BLOCK,
1 SKIP), which the dashboard cannot show for a past day, and a fifth variant of
the dashboard-semantics defect: at a day boundary the today and attention lines
vanish rather than reading zero, so a reader sees no outcome mix at all. The same
boundary confirmed the 15:15Z prediction -- the untriaged count stayed at 17 for
six hours after the triage merged and cleared only at midnight.

